        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles a hardcoded/weak Bearer-token credential check (a 'cp_<prefix>_<secret>' token parsed straight from the Authorization header, with names like prefix/secret) that a scanner might flag as broken auth or hardcoded-secret comparison. Actually safe: the secret is never compared as a literal in code; it is verified against a stored hash via key.verify() -> Django check_password() (constant-time, salted hash, accounts/models.py:157-159). The lookup is a parameterized ORM filter on prefix with revoked_at__isnull check, and the owner must still be active and staff-role. No plaintext secret, no string equality, no injection."
      },
      "false_positive_trap": true,
