        "description": "Resembles SQL injection: raw user query-string input (request.GET 'q' and 'insurance') is fed into a database filter, which scanners flag as user-input-into-query. Actually safe: the values go through the Django ORM as Q(field__icontains=q) parameters, which are bound/escaped by the ORM rather than string-concatenated into SQL. There is no .raw()/.extra()/cursor.execute and no f-string/format SQL. The base queryset is also tenant/permission-scoped via visible_patient_queryset(request.user), so it cannot widen visibility."
